  "title": "3-Edge-Coloring Conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture Suppose $G$ with $|V(G)|>2$ is a connected cubic graph admitting a $3$-edge coloring. Then there is an edge $e \\in E(G)$ such that the cubic graph homeomorphic to $G-e$ has a $3$-edge coloring.",
